<!-- The N.D. Cal. bankruptcy adversary complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs)
     in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; Civil L.R. 3-4(c)(2)(A), applied by B.L.R. 1001-2: a
     standard proportional font) at 12 pt (size 24 half points, Civil L.R. 3-4(c)(2)(B)); Body Text and the headings
     in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch, the numbered lines of the pleading paper, Civil L.R. 3-4(c)(2)); single
     lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single). The page (letter, top and bottom margins 1 in, left 1.5 in, right
     1 in, the rules beside the text) and the footer (the line numbers, the page number, the paper's title and case
     number from the sample) are written by docx/canb.lua (FORMBOOK_FINAL, FORMBOOK_FOOTERS), as is every
     paragraph's own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="24" body="480" single="240" indent="720" heading="480" heading-before="0" heading-after="0">
</reference>
